From 496998928c3deb782eb101f7c0027ae9c8e7812c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ettore Di Giacinto <mudler@localai.io>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:10:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu: keep partial sums in the SVE ggml_vec_dot_f32 tail

The SVE leftover path of ggml_vec_dot_f32 used
svmad_f32_m(pg, ax1, ay1, sum1). The merging form keeps the first
operand in inactive lanes, so those lanes of sum1 were replaced by the
zero-filled load. Every dot product whose length is not a multiple of
the SVE vector width lost part of its sum.

F32 matrix products with such inner lengths use this path on SVE CPUs.
On a 128-bit SVE CPU a product of length 37 had a relative error of
about 0.4. HTDemucs is affected through the 1x1 convolutions in its
outermost DConv blocks, which reduce over 6 channels. With the CPU
backend on 128-bit SVE, the "other", "drums" and "bass" stems took 7 to
14 dB of extra energy, and their correlation with the PyTorch stems fell
to between 0.005 and 0.36. x86 CPUs and Arm CPUs without SVE use other
code and are not affected.

Use svmla_f32_m(pg, sum1, ax1, ay1), which keeps sum1 in inactive
lanes. This is the same change as upstream llama.cpp #24699. After the
change, HTDemucs on emulated 128-bit SVE gives the same stems as on x86.

This patch carries only the vec.cpp change. Drop it once the vendored
ggml in audio.cpp has the fix.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-sonnet-5-5
---
 external/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/external/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.cpp b/external/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.cpp
index 0d42f4ed..d54f9e14 100644
--- a/external/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.cpp
+++ b/external/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.cpp
@@ -75,12 +75,12 @@ void ggml_vec_dot_f32(int n, float * GGML_RESTRICT s, size_t bs, const float * G
             ay1 = GGML_F32_VEC_LOAD(y + i);
             sum1 = GGML_F32_VEC_FMA(sum1, ax1, ay1);
         }
-        // maximum number of leftover elements will be less that ggml_f32_epr. Apply predicated svmad on available elements only
+        // maximum number of leftover elements will be less that ggml_f32_epr. Apply predicated svmla on available elements only
         if (np2 < n) {
             svbool_t pg = svwhilelt_b32(np2, n);
             ax1 = svld1_f32(pg, x + np2);
             ay1 = svld1_f32(pg, y + np2);
-            sum1 = svmad_f32_m(pg, ax1, ay1, sum1);
+            sum1 = svmla_f32_m(pg, sum1, ax1, ay1);
         }
         // reduce sum1,sum2 to sum1
         GGML_F32_VEC_REDUCE(sumf, sum1, sum2, sum3, sum4, sum5, sum6, sum7, sum8);
